---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import geometryFigure from '../assets/realized-deformation-geometry.webp';
import stellarFigure from '../assets/representative-stellar-sequences.webp';
import thermodynamicFigure from '../assets/thermodynamic-propagation.webp';
import { REPOSITORIES } from '../site';

const licenseUrl = 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/';
---

<section class="section visual-story" aria-labelledby="visual-story-title">
	<div class="shell">
		<div class="visual-story-heading">
			<div>
				<p class="section-kicker">Method in three stages</p>
				<h2 id="visual-story-title">From a local change to a stellar response.</h2>
			</div>
			<p>
				Three released calculation figures trace the method from deformation geometry through
				thermodynamic reconstruction to stellar and tidal response.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="story-stages">
			<article class="story-stage">
				<div class="story-copy">
					<p class="stage-number">01 · Define</p>
					<h3>Make the intervention explicit.</h3>
					<p>
						A Gaussian unit shape is introduced through a smooth activation window. Signed
						amplitudes then produce a controlled family of raw sound-speed profiles on the
						declared domain.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="story-figure">
					<Picture
						src={geometryFigure}
						formats={['avif', 'webp']}
						widths={[720, 1200, 1800]}
						sizes="(max-width: 860px) calc(100vw - 2rem), 66vw"
						alt="Four panels show the Gaussian and smooth window used to define the deformation, the realized unit deformation, signed changes to squared sound speed, and representative raw BSk24 sound-speed profiles."
						loading="lazy"
						decoding="async"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						Realized deformation geometry. The construction is an effective controlled
						deformation, not a microscopic composition model. <a href={REPOSITORIES.eosCampaignRelease}>Open original release</a>.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</article>

			<article class="story-stage">
				<div class="story-copy">
					<p class="stage-number">02 · Reconstruct</p>
					<h3>Require thermodynamic consistency.</h3>
					<p>
						Only admitted raw proposals are reconstructed. The plots expose how the signed
						sound-speed change accumulates into pressure and the effective one-fluid density
						and chemical-potential relations.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="story-figure">
					<Picture
						src={thermodynamicFigure}
						formats={['avif', 'webp']}
						widths={[720, 1200, 1800]}
						sizes="(max-width: 860px) calc(100vw - 2rem), 66vw"
						alt="Six plots compare negative, zero, and positive BSk24 sound-speed deformations: the local signed change accumulates into pressure differences and shifts reconstructed density and chemical-potential relations."
						loading="lazy"
						decoding="async"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						Thermodynamic propagation for representative accepted branch endpoints. These are
						effective one-fluid reconstructions. <a href={REPOSITORIES.eosCampaignRelease}>Open original release</a>.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</article>

			<article class="story-stage">
				<div class="story-copy">
					<p class="stage-number">03 · Propagate</p>
					<h3>Resolve the macroscopic response.</h3>
					<p>
						Representative admitted branches show how softening and stiffening alter
						mass–radius sequences, the quadrupolar Love number, and tidal deformability—while
						retaining numerical endpoint status in the figure itself.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="story-figure">
					<Picture
						src={stellarFigure}
						formats={['avif', 'webp']}
						widths={[720, 1200, 1800]}
						sizes="(max-width: 860px) calc(100vw - 2rem), 66vw"
						alt="Six panels compare softening and stiffening BSk24 branches in mass–radius, Love-number, and tidal-deformability sequences; blue curves soften, red curves stiffen, and symbols distinguish refined turning points from retained-domain endpoints."
						loading="lazy"
						decoding="async"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						Representative stellar and tidal sequences. Filled circles mark saved refined
						turning points; diamonds mark retained-domain endpoints, which are not interchangeable
						maximum-mass determinations. <a href={REPOSITORIES.eosCampaignRelease}>Open original release</a>.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</article>
		</div>

		<p class="figure-credit">
			Figures: Ioannis Papathanasiou,{' '}
			<a href={REPOSITORIES.eosCampaignRelease}>BSk24 campaign data v1.0.0</a>,{' '}
			<a href={licenseUrl}>CC BY 4.0</a>. Web-optimized from the released PDFs with
			scientific content unchanged.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>
